From 09ff3ed553ba97f5fd5a880ab4197d3209a83d0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:19:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Linux: hold on an unknown host wallet policy instead of
 releasing the lease

hostWalletRefusal folded UNKNOWN (no RPC quorum, an expired snapshot, an unloadable policy) into a REFUSAL, so an
external RPC outage made renewLeases and auditClaims retire AND release every wallet-gated lease (reserve gas spent
and the deployment re-claimed), the share-resize path evict-and-release, and the gate answer 403. The Windows node
distinguishes the two (#walletPolicyState); Linux now does too, through the shared admission's decision():

- hostWalletDecision -> {refusal} | {unknown} | allowed until validUntil (the decision's chain deadline). Same
  classification as Windows ("catalog app reference required" is the policy's own refusal); an older bundle without
  decision() is unknown, loudly.
- definite refusal (host owner policy or platform moderation): unchanged - stop + prove + release.
- unknown (walletHoldLocal): stop serving here exactly as a retire stops it (Linux has no network hold
  acknowledgement), record terminal + walletHeld, lease KEPT: no release, renewal or re-claim. The held id is not
  vouched for as an unresumed lease, so the reconciler finishes an unconfirmed stop.
- held records on each audit pass (walletHeldReview): lease gone -> drop the hold; owner stop / pin elsewhere /
  definite refusal -> release (no final proof: nothing was served while held); unknown -> stay held (retry an
  unconfirmed stop); allowed -> clear, and the claim sweep's existing resume path (all claim gates, no tx) serves it.
- gateAppReference: unknown -> 503 wallet_policy_unavailable (version switch defers instead of evicting).
- tryClaim: a fresh wallet decision after the prefetch for claims and resumes.
- every lease send on a wallet decision (renew, lapsed re-claim, audit re-acquire, claim) carries a send-time gate,
  re-checked when the operator queue reaches it (sendLeaseTx/sendOperatorTx opts.gate): held meanwhile or past the
  decision deadline -> not signed or relayed (superseded).

Tests: test/supervisor-wallet-unknown-hold.test.mjs runs the real supervisor functions with the real shipped
admission bundle; test/supervisor-wallet-policy.test.mjs adapted to decision() (and its pre-existing missing-global
failure fixed).
